<title>SPAIN: Santander 9-mo attributable up 13.22 pct.</title>
<headline>Santander 9-mo attributable up 13.22 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to end September</p>
<p>				    (billion pesetas, unless stated)</p>
<p> Net attributable			 71.78   vs   63.40</p>
<p> Pretax profit/loss		    134.82   vs  106.54</p>
<p> Net taxed				  98.42   vs   83.22</p>
<p> Net interest income		   292.70   vs  260.10</p>
<p> Fee income				116.15   vs  101.35</p>
<p> Other financial/trading income     52.26   vs   35.10</p>
<p> Ordinary margin			 461.11   vs  396.54</p>
<p> Operating expenses		   -285.71   vs  -259.21</p>
<p> Operating income			136.15   vs   102.37</p>
<p> Net loan loss provs		   -32.78   vs   -24.76</p>
<p> Extraordinary gains		    11.01   vs     9.61</p>
<p> Interim dividend/share		 70 pta  up  11.11 pct</p>
<p> Non-perfoming loans coverage ration:</p>
<p>						91.72   vs  86.29</p>
<p> Return on assets (percent)	    0.73   vs   0.71</p>
<p> Reutrn on equity (percent)	   17.56   vs  16.55</p>
<p> Loans				   7,437.65   vs  6,191.64</p>
<p> Deposits			     10,588.34   vs  9,198.14</p>
<p> Total assets			 18,977.01   vs 16,443.18</p>
<p> Equity				    612.10   vs    565.06</p>
<p> BIS capital adequacy ratio	   11.86   vs     10.92</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Spanish bank is Banco Santander</p>
</text>
